# meta: !!omap
# - {description: 'Fitted per-frame payload pointing offsets of the ESIS-I flight, relative to the reference fit, one row per frame of
#     esis.flights.f1.data.level_1(). The offsets are common to all four channels (a rigid-payload model); z_primary is the focus of each
#     channel''s sector of the primary at the field stop, measured from the channels against one another and applied here, which moves
#     each channel''s sky along its dispersion without moving the windows.  drift_x and drift_y are the measured motion of each channel''s
#     windows from their flight median, and yaw_grating and pitch_grating the per-channel grating offsets that reproduce it.'}
